@* HelpMembersPage: help topic "Managing project members" at "/help/project-members". Static text. *@
@page "/help/project-members"

<HelpTopicFrame Slug="project-members">
    <section class="card">
        <p>Ordinary users see only the projects they belong to; system administrators see all projects. A
            <strong>project admin</strong> (and any system administrator)
            manages the members from the <strong>Members</strong> section of the project page.</p>
        <h2>Add someone who has an account</h2>
        <p>Choose <strong>+ Add member</strong>, type the exact user name and choose whether the person is a project
            admin. There is no list of users to pick from, so ask the person for their user name. If the name cannot
            be added you get one message whatever the reason (a misspelled name, an account that does not exist or
            one that is disabled), and repeated failures are recorded in the audit trail and slow you down for a few
            minutes.</p>
        <h2>Create an account for someone new</h2>
        <p>On the <strong>Add member</strong> page choose <strong>Create a new account</strong>. Enter a user name and
            a display name. The account is created together with the membership, and ReviewCenter shows a temporary
            password <strong>once</strong>. Give it to the person right away; it cannot be shown again. At the first
            sign-in the person must choose a new password before doing anything else.</p>
        <h2>Change a role or remove a member</h2>
        <p>Use <strong>Make project admin</strong>, <strong>Make member</strong> or <strong>Remove</strong> on a
            member. A project always keeps at least one project admin: a project admin cannot remove or demote the
            last one, even themselves. A system administrator can.</p>
        <h2>Reviewers who are removed</h2>
        <p>A reviewer slot keeps its reviewer when the person is removed from the project. The review page marks the
            reviewer as <strong>No longer a project member</strong>, and that reviewer cannot sign until added
            again.</p>
        <h2>Project audit trail</h2>
        <p>The <strong>Audit trail</strong> button of the project page shows everything recorded for this project,
            including every member change and every change of the evidence settings.</p>
        <h2>Evidence settings</h2>
        <p>Only a project admin or a system administrator can open the <strong>Evidence settings</strong> button of
            the project page. A plain member cannot see it. See <a href="/help/evidence-settings">Evidence
            settings</a>.</p>
        <h2>Review rules</h2>
        <p>The <strong>Review rules</strong> card of the project page, also only for a project admin or a system
            administrator, switches on or off whether the person who created a review may also be one of its
            reviewers. It is on by default, and every change is recorded in the audit trail.</p>
    </section>
</HelpTopicFrame>
